            "**Plan.** Agree in part. Line of argument: crisis was *necessary* in all three cases but not *sufficient* — weak government and determined leadership turned crisis into dictatorship. Use one paragraph per factor, comparing all three dictators each time.",
            "**Paragraph 1 — crisis (agree).** Crisis was essential in every case. The Great Depression left around 6 million Germans unemployed by 1932 and Nazi votes rose sharply; Japan's invasion and civil war wrecked Nationalist China; and in Cambodia the Vietnam War and US bombing between 1969 and 1973 created anger and refugees that the Khmer Rouge used to recruit. Without these crises, none of the three would probably have gained power.",
            "**Paragraph 2 — weak government.** However, crisis alone was not enough: governments that could have solved the crisis would have survived. Weimar's coalitions collapsed into rule by decree; Chiang Kai-shek's government was seen as corrupt; Lon Nol's Khmer Republic depended on US aid. In each case the government's weakness let the crisis turn into a collapse of authority.",
